Sustainability is revolutionizing the real estate sector, with a growing focus on energy-efficient designs, renewable energy adoption, and climate-resilient construction. Developers are prioritizing eco-friendly initiatives, in line with increasing consumer demand and regulatory advancements.\n\nAt ANAX Holding, we are taking proactive steps toward sustainability. Our upcoming Evora Residences in Al Furjan will incorporate solar panels, marking a significant stride toward energy efficiency. With government incentives supporting solar energy adoption, we anticipate a widespread shift towards greener developments, making sustainability a core aspect of future projects.\n\nTechnology Driving Transformation ', 397, '749a9eacfa52594fb08e3ecd78425f09', NULL, '', 0, '2026-10-08 06:41:26'),
(6309, 'blog', '167', 1, 'article', 'Dubai Real Estate Trends for 2025: Expert Insights from Leading Developers', 'our-blogs/dubai-real-estate-trends-for-2025-expert-insights-from-leading-developers', 'Blog: Dubai Real Estate Trends for 2025: Expert Insights from Leading Developers (published 2025-01-18)\nImran Khan, CEO & Founder, PIXL Group, expressed; Technology is reshaping the real estate industry, optimizing efficiency and unlocking new business opportunities. Over recent years, tech-driven solutions have streamlined operations, enhanced customer experiences, and provided valuable market insights through data analytics.\n\nAt PIXL Group, we’ve undergone a significant transformation, evolving from a lead generation company in 2019 to a full-service proptech firm. We now specialize in CRM marketing, web services, and market intelligence. However, technology alone is not enough—it’s how effectively we integrate it into our processes that determines success. The future belongs to those who embrace innovation and leverage tech to enhance profitability and client satisfaction.\n\nMarket Growth & Emerging Trends \n\nRamjee Iyer, Chairman & MD, Acube Developments said, Dubai’s real estate market has experienced impressive growth, with sales and rental prices surging in 2024—Dubai saw a 21% increase in sale and rental prices, while Abu Dhabi recorded a 7% rise in sales and a 4% rental hike.\n\nThis growth is fueled by foreign investments, government initiatives, and economic diversification. Additionally, wellness-focused developments and eco-conscious communities are becoming increasingly popular, as buyers prioritize health and sustainability.', 365, '545e71121478eb4bb677ef0dbdb0d04d', NULL, '', 0, '2026-10-08 06:41:26'),
(6310, 'blog', '167', 2, 'article', 'Dubai Real Estate Trends for 2025: Expert Insights from Leading Developers', 'our-blogs/dubai-real-estate-trends-for-2025-expert-insights-from-leading-developers', 'Blog: Dubai Real Estate Trends for 2025: Expert Insights from Leading Developers (published 2025-01-18)\nIn 2025, we anticipate a stronger demand for smart homes and mixed-use developments that integrate residential, commercial, and retail spaces. The market’s future lies in sustainable, tech-enabled properties offering lifestyle value and long-term investment potential.\n\nLuxury Market & Investment Appeal\n \n\nYogesh Bulchandani, CEO, Sunrise Capital expressed, Dubai remains a premier destination for real estate investment, offering lucrative rental yields between 5% and 9%. The rise of branded residences is a notable trend, reflecting the city’s appeal to high-net-worth investors seeking exclusivity and premium living.\n\nOff-plan sales continue to flourish, driven by growing investor confidence. Today’s buyers are highly informed and prioritize quality over cost savings, emphasizing superior craftsmanship and reputable developers. With a balanced supply-and-demand dynamic, along with supportive regulatory policies, Dubai’s market is expected to witness further price growth, particularly in the off-plan segment.\n\nAffordable Housing: A Growing Segment \n\nHumera Khan, General Manager, Al Zarooni Developments said, Affordable housing is emerging as a critical growth sector in 2025. There remains a significant demand for well-designed, cost-effective properties in areas such as Dubai Sports City, Al Furjan, and Arjan. As supply struggles to meet demand, this segment presents a valuable opportunity for investors to achieve strong returns.', 389, '85cb279f86cad6c3d3284e6d9beeab22', NULL, '', 0, '2026-10-08 06:41:26'),
(6311, 'blog', '167', 3, 'article', 'Dubai Real Estate Trends for 2025: Expert Insights from Leading Developers', 'our-blogs/dubai-real-estate-trends-for-2025-expert-insights-from-leading-developers', 'Blog: Dubai Real Estate Trends for 2025: Expert Insights from Leading Developers (published 2025-01-18)\nAt Al Zarooni Developments, we are addressing this demand with our All Seasons Residences project in Dubai Sports City. Beyond profitability, this initiative aligns with our vision of fostering inclusive communities and creating sustainable, long-term investment prospects.\n\nLuxury & Ultra-Luxury Market Expansion \n\nSrishti Gaur, Head of Marketing & Media Relations, Arista Properties expressed; The high-end property segment is set to dominate Dubai’s real estate landscape in 2025. Last year alone, transaction volumes in this segment increased by 35% year-on-year, reinforcing Dubai’s status as a global luxury destination.\n\nWith surging demand, areas like Dubai Marina, Meydan, MBR City, and Palm Jumeirah continue to attract elite buyers. At Arista Properties, we’re catering to this growing segment with our Wadi Villas project, offering ultra-luxurious residences that combine exclusivity, state-of-the-art amenities, and architectural brilliance.\n\nFor ultra-high-net-worth individuals (UHNWIs), luxury real estate isn’t just about status—it’s about acquiring assets that appreciate in value while delivering unparalleled living experiences.\n\nConclusion: A Year of Innovation & Growth', 324, 'acedb78f0f9c58dd8815f05cb417a0f7', NULL, '', 0, '2026-10-08 06:41:26'),
(6312, 'blog', '167', 4, 'article', 'Dubai Real Estate Trends for 2025: Expert Insights from Leading Developers', 'our-blogs/dubai-real-estate-trends-for-2025-expert-insights-from-leading-developers', 'Blog: Dubai Real Estate Trends for 2025: Expert Insights from Leading Developers (published 2025-01-18)\nDubai’s real estate sector is set for a transformative year in 2025, characterized by sustainability, technological advancements, and evolving consumer preferences. With strategic investments, regulatory support, and strong market fundamentals, the emirate continues to cement its position as a global real estate hub. Whether through eco-friendly projects, smart homes, or luxury developments, the future of Dubai’s property market is dynamic and full of potential.\n\nSource: Gulf Business', 149, '850b6374695856f70f2043e2cd49b1ff', NULL, '', 0, '2026-10-08 06:41:26'),
(6313, 'blog', '168', 0, 'article', 'Dubai Real Estate Breaks Records as Prices Soar to New Heights', 'our-blogs/dubai-real-estate-breaks-records-as-prices-soar-to-new-heights', 'Blog: Dubai Real Estate Breaks Records as Prices Soar to New Heights (published 2025-03-16)\nDubai\'s real estate market continues to defy global economic challenges, posting unprecedented growth in February 2025. Sales volumes, prices, and investor activity reached new records, highlighting the city\'s appeal as a global investment powerhouse.\n\nDriven by a thriving economy, increasing population, and strategic government policies, Dubai’s real estate market has firmly established itself as a top destination for investors worldwide. February saw property sales surge to Dh41 billion, a 17% month-on-month (MoM) increase, with 14,929 transactions—up 15% from January.\n\nRecord-Breaking Prices\n\nThe average price per square foot reached a historic Dh1,505, marking a 1.41% MoM increase (Dh20.94). This price point more than doubles the market\'s lowest point of Dh716 in 2019, further signaling Dubai’s remarkable recovery. Off-plan properties continue to dominate, making up 59% of all transactions, showing strong investor confidence in the city\'s long-term growth prospects.\n\nThe luxury sector remains a standout performer, with villa prices soaring 60% MoM to an average of Dh11.48 million, while apartments saw a 30% rise to Dh2.26 million. Key neighbourhoods driving this growth include Motor City, Jumeirah Village Circle (JVC), and Dubai Marina for apartments, and Jumeirah Golf Estates, The Villa, and Meadows for villas.\n\nEconomic Resilience and Population Growth', 368, 'aa13dfebdb0a7b72df1c3e3d714a9e01', NULL, '', 0, '2026-10-08 06:41:26'),
(6314, 'blog', '168', 1, 'article', 'Dubai Real Estate Breaks Records as Prices Soar to New Heights', 'our-blogs/dubai-real-estate-breaks-records-as-prices-soar-to-new-heights', 'Blog: Dubai Real Estate Breaks Records as Prices Soar to New Heights (published 2025-03-16)\nDubai’s economic resilience is a key driver of the real estate boom. The city’s GDP grew by 4.2% in 2024, outperforming global averages, and the population surged to 4.2 million—a 6% year-on-year increase. This growth is largely attributed to skilled expatriates and entrepreneurs taking advantage of Dubai’s golden visa program and tax-free incentives. Government initiatives like the Dubai 2040 Urban Master Plan, which focuses on sustainable infrastructure and community-driven developments, have further enhanced the city’s attractiveness to investors.\n\nIndustry experts highlight that Dubai’s real estate market is not merely recovering but reshaping itself. “Pro-business policies, top-tier infrastructure, and a rise in high-net-worth individuals moving from Europe and Asia have created the perfect environment for growth,” said a property market analyst.\n\nThe Shift Towards Homeownership\n\nSkyrocketing rental prices have prompted a shift toward homeownership. Average annual rents for apartments and villas increased by 22% and 28%, respectively, in 2024, driving more residents to invest in property. Betterhomes reported a 25% MoM increase in buyer leads, with end-users now accounting for 53% of transactions—signifying a shift from the investor-heavy market of the past.', 344, '480595f826c988c1e1366513ba837b49', NULL, '', 0, '2026-10-08 06:41:26'),
(6315, 'blog', '168', 2, 'article', 'Dubai Real Estate Breaks Records as Prices Soar to New Heights', 'our-blogs/dubai-real-estate-breaks-records-as-prices-soar-to-new-heights', 'Blog: Dubai Real Estate Breaks Records as Prices Soar to New Heights (published 2025-03-16)\nChristopher Cina, Director of Sales at Betterhomes, noted that this uptick in first-time buyers reflects a broader change in Dubai’s identity. “Dubai is no longer just a transient hub; it’s becoming a place where people want to put down roots. Communities with integrated amenities, like Dubai Hills Estate and Palm Jumeirah, are particularly in demand.”\n\nOff-Plan Properties Dominate the Market\n\nOff-plan properties were the main driver of February\'s sales activity. Leading developers such as Emaar (Dh4.11 billion), Sobha Group (Dh1.44 billion), and Damac Properties (Dh0.82 billion) played key roles in this surge. International investors made up 35% of transactions, with Russians, Indians, and British nationals topping the list of buyers.\n\nJaykrishnan Bhaskar, a property consultant, commented, “Dubai’s off-plan market offers unrivaled returns on investment. Projects near Expo City Dubai and Al Qudra’s eco-friendly districts are particularly attractive to ESG-focused buyers, who value sustainability alongside luxury.”\n\nFinancing as a Growth Catalyst\n\nDespite rising property prices, mortgage transactions accounted for 64% of all sales. This surge can be attributed to attractive lending rates, with banks offering mortgages as low as 3.5% for expatriates. The UAE Central Bank’s decision to keep interest rates low in 2024 has ensured that financing remains accessible, with banks offering flexible payment plans for off-plan properties.', 386, 'b8c1a26a440d4b11fa1644605934a39b', NULL, '', 0, '2026-10-08 06:41:26'),
(6316, 'blog', '168', 3, 'article', 'Dubai Real Estate Breaks Records as Prices Soar to New Heights', 'our-blogs/dubai-real-estate-breaks-records-as-prices-soar-to-new-heights', 'Blog: Dubai Real Estate Breaks Records as Prices Soar to New Heights (published 2025-03-16)\n“Financing is no longer a hurdle—it’s become a catalyst for growth,” said the Head of Mortgage Solutions at a leading bank. “First-time buyers can secure homes with down payments as low as 15%, while investors can expand their portfolios with attractive financing terms.”\n\nDubai\'s Real Estate Outlook for 2025 and Beyond\n\nThe real estate market shows no signs of slowing down. With Expo City Dubai boosting tourism and the non-oil economy now contributing 78% of Dubai’s GDP, analysts predict a 12–18% increase in property prices in 2025. Mega-projects like the Dh30 billion Marsa Al Arab waterfront development are expected to continue driving growth.\n\n“Dubai is not just competing with other global property markets; it’s setting a new benchmark,” said Bhaskar. “The city’s blend of innovation, stability, and ambition positions it as the ultimate safe haven for investors.”\n\nAs Dubai’s skyline continues to expand, its real estate market is not just growing in size but evolving to be smarter, greener, and more inclusive—solidifying its place as the world’s most dynamic property market.\n\nIn addition to February’s impressive performance, January saw Dubai’s real estate market post strong numbers, with property sales totaling Dh51.1 billion—a 39.91% increase compared to the same month last year. A report from fäm Properties revealed that February\'s 16,099 transactions represented a 35.5% increase in volume compared to February 2024, making it one of the best months on record.\n\nSource: Khaleej Times', 401, '3b8055d5af183f83c0d176d79e90627d', NULL, '', 0, '2026-10-08 06:41:26'),
(6317, 'blog', '169', 0, 'article', 'Dubai Unveils Pilot Phase of Real Estate Tokenisation Project to Attract Investment', 'our-blogs/dubai-unveils-pilot-phase-of-real-estate-tokenisation-project-to-attract-investment', 'Blog: Dubai Unveils Pilot Phase of Real Estate Tokenisation Project to Attract Investment (published 2025-03-20)\nDubai has officially launched the pilot phase of its real estate tokenisation project, aiming to bolster investment in the city’s property market amid its ongoing boom. This initiative is designed to revolutionise property transactions by converting real estate assets into digital tokens, recorded on blockchain technology, which streamlines the buying, selling, and investing process.\n\nMarwan bin Ghalita, Director-General of the Dubai Land Department (DLD), highlighted the project’s potential, stating, “In this era of rapid technological growth, real estate tokenisation stands as a game-changing tool, transforming how the sector operates.”\n\nTokenisation allows fractional ownership of properties, where assets are broken into smaller units (tokens) based on investors’ financial capacities. This opens the door for multiple investors to own portions of a single property, thus lowering the entry barriers for those interested in property investment.\n\nThe DLD aims for the tokenisation project to significantly expand Dubai’s real estate investment landscape, attracting global technology firms and broadening access to the property market. It is projected that the tokenisation market in Dubai will hit Dh60 billion ($16.33 billion) by 2033, which could account for 7% of the city\'s total real estate transactions.', 359, '1b30dc2931a35f506b594acc93b27221', NULL, '', 0, '2026-10-08 06:41:26'),
(6318, 'blog', '169', 1, 'article', 'Dubai Unveils Pilot Phase of Real Estate Tokenisation Project to Attract Investment', 'our-blogs/dubai-unveils-pilot-phase-of-real-estate-tokenisation-project-to-attract-investment', 'Blog: Dubai Unveils Pilot Phase of Real Estate Tokenisation Project to Attract Investment (published 2025-03-20)\nThis announcement follows a robust performance in Dubai’s property market, with real estate transactions surging by 20% in 2024, totalling Dh761 billion. Additionally, the number of transactions increased by 36%, reaching 226,000, alongside record-breaking sales of homes priced above $10 million. Dubai’s property market is experiencing sustained growth, driven by government initiatives like residency programs for retirees and remote workers, the expansion of the 10-year golden visa, and broader economic diversification.\n\nIn addition to tokenisation, the DLD has launched various initiatives to further support property sector growth, including a smart rental index system and new freehold ownership opportunities for property owners in specific areas like Sheikh Zayed Road and Al Jaddaf.\n\nWhy Is Real Estate Tokenisation Gaining Traction?\n\nTokenisation is gaining significant momentum within the real estate industry as developers partner with technology providers to explore new ways of fractionalising both debt and equity. Essentially, tokenisation enables the representation of physical property or its cash flow on the blockchain, offering the same potential for income generation as traditional assets but with added benefits.', 338, '4da94d7aa6d91c13781203713045841f', NULL, '', 0, '2026-10-08 06:41:26'),
(6319, 'blog', '169', 2, 'article', 'Dubai Unveils Pilot Phase of Real Estate Tokenisation Project to Attract Investment', 'our-blogs/dubai-unveils-pilot-phase-of-real-estate-tokenisation-project-to-attract-investment', 'Blog: Dubai Unveils Pilot Phase of Real Estate Tokenisation Project to Attract Investment (published 2025-03-20)\nOne of the key advantages of tokenisation is the increased liquidity it offers, which makes real estate investments more accessible and efficient. By reducing transaction and administrative costs, it opens the door to fractional ownership, allowing investors to purchase shares of a property that align with their financial capabilities.\n\nAdditionally, the use of blockchain technology adds transparency, speeds up transactions, and eliminates intermediary costs and fees. Analysts note that tokenisation also mitigates the complexities of traditional real estate transactions, such as notary visits, transaction costs, and land transfer taxes, making them less relevant or even obsolete.\n\nKPMG has pointed out that tokenisation is particularly beneficial for owners of individual assets or smaller portfolios. It provides a more affordable and efficient means of offering fractional ownership and facilitating secondary trading.\n\nThrough these innovations, real estate tokenisation is poised to make property ownership more accessible to a wider range of investors, reshaping the future of property investment globally.\n\nSource: The National News', 315, '7078a6bc2b11ac06d23aa7d1e79a29df', NULL, '', 0, '2026-10-08 06:41:26'),
(6320, 'blog', '170', 0, 'article', 'Nshama Launches Exciting New Project – Holland Gardens at Town Square Dubai', 'our-blogs/nshama-launches-exciting-new-project-holland-gardens-at-town-square-dubai', 'Blog: Nshama Launches Exciting New Project – Holland Gardens at Town Square Dubai (published 2023-05-12)\nNshama, a renowned developer in the real estate industry, has recently launched an exciting new project called Holland Gardens at Town Square, Dubai. This highly anticipated development is set to redefine modern living in Dubai, offering residents a vibrant community surrounded by an array of amenities and conveniences. Presenting spacious studios, 1, 2, 3 bedroom & duplex apartments at Town Square Dubai. This features a fully fitted kitchen modern interior layout and the perfect combination of style and functionality. Here, we will delve into the details of Holland Gardens and explore why it has become a top choice for homebuyers and investors alike.\n\nHolland Gardens is strategically located within Town Square, one of Dubai’s most sought-after residential communities. Situated at the intersection of Al Qudra Road and Emirates Road, residents will enjoy seamless connectivity to major landmarks and key destinations in the city. With its proximity to schools, hospitals, retail outlets, and recreational facilities, this development offers a truly convenient lifestyle.\n\nNshama’s commitment to excellence is evident in the design and architecture of Holland Gardens. The project boasts contemporary and sophisticated designs, with an emphasis on spaciousness and functionality. The apartments feature high-quality finishes and smart layouts that maximize natural light and create a welcoming ambience for residents.', 383, 'b67e09824b44bf2e26b131c3feae8b1a', NULL, '', 0, '2026-10-08 06:41:26'),
(6321, 'blog', '170', 1, 'article', 'Nshama Launches Exciting New Project – Holland Gardens at Town Square Dubai', 'our-blogs/nshama-launches-exciting-new-project-holland-gardens-at-town-square-dubai', 'Blog: Nshama Launches Exciting New Project – Holland Gardens at Town Square Dubai (published 2023-05-12)\nHolland Gardens aims to provide residents with an unparalleled living experience. The community is equipped with an array of amenities, including swimming pools, fitness centres, jogging tracks, parks, and playgrounds. Moreover, residents will have access to Town Square’s impressive Central Park, which spans over 50,000 square meters and offers a variety of recreational activities.\n\nNshama understands the importance of a vibrant lifestyle, and Holland Gardens delivers just that. The community is designed to foster a sense of belonging and social engagement among residents. The town centre features a wide range of retail outlets, dining options, and entertainment venues, ensuring that there is always something to explore and enjoy.\n\nFor those considering invest in real estate, Holland Gardens presents an attractive opportunity. Nshama has a proven track record of delivering successful projects, and Town Square has established itself as a highly desirable location for both residents and investors. The development’s promising rental yields and potential for capital appreciation make it an appealing choice for individuals seeking long-term gains.', 317, 'db83fd4e138d2808d0a1bf4ba74addc4', NULL, '', 0, '2026-10-08 06:41:26'),
(6322, 'blog', '170', 2, 'article', 'Nshama Launches Exciting New Project – Holland Gardens at Town Square Dubai', 'our-blogs/nshama-launches-exciting-new-project-holland-gardens-at-town-square-dubai', 'Blog: Nshama Launches Exciting New Project – Holland Gardens at Town Square Dubai (published 2023-05-12)\nOverall, Nshama’s launch of Holland Gardens at Town Square has created a buzz in the Dubai real estate market. With its prime location, thoughtful design, abundant amenities, and promising investment potential, this development offers a truly exceptional living experience. Whether you are looking for your dream home or a lucrative investment opportunity, Holland Gardens should definitely be on your radar. Stay tuned for more updates on this exciting project.', 142, '02deb4a9c86de3d75b57eda7406cfe83', NULL, '', 0, '2026-10-08 06:41:26'),
(6323, 'blog', '171', 0, 'article', 'The Highly Anticipated Marriott Residences is All Set To Be Launched At Business Bay', 'our-blogs/marriott-residences-is-all-set-to-be-launched-at-business-bay', 'Blog: The Highly Anticipated Marriott Residences is All Set To Be Launched At Business Bay (published 2023-05-13)\nIn an exciting development in the Dubai real estate market, Fortune 5 is thrilled to announce the launch of the highly anticipated Marriott Residences at Business Bay. This prestigious project combines exceptional luxury living in the heart of Dubai’s bustling business district. Presenting opulent and beautifully designed 1 and 2-bedroom apartments. With a commitment to offering world-class amenities and unparalleled comfort, the Marriott Residences at Business Bay is set to redefine upscale living in the city.\n\nSituated in the prestigious Business Bay district, the Marriott Residences boast a prime location that puts residents at the centre of Dubai’s thriving business hub. The area offers excellent connectivity and easy access to major commercial, leisure, and entertainment destinations, making it an ideal choice for professionals and families alike.\n\nThe Marriott Residences at Business Bay feature a striking architectural design that exudes elegance and sophistication. The development offers a range of meticulously crafted apartments, each thoughtfully designed to provide residents with an exquisite living experience. The interiors boast contemporary styling, high-quality finishes, and a seamless blend of comfort and functionality.', 342, 'acd518923ccd5a75d3104fe1ea11eca4', NULL, '', 0, '2026-10-08 06:41:26'),
(6324, 'blog', '171', 1, 'article', 'The Highly Anticipated Marriott Residences is All Set To Be Launched At Business Bay', 'our-blogs/marriott-residences-is-all-set-to-be-launched-at-business-bay', 'Blog: The Highly Anticipated Marriott Residences is All Set To Be Launched At Business Bay (published 2023-05-13)\nResidents of the Marriott Residences will enjoy an array of world-class amenities and services that cater to their every need. From state-of-the-art fitness facilities and swimming pools to valet service, pool deck with loungers, multipurpose podium, and children’s play area, every aspect of luxurious living has been carefully considered. Additionally, a dedicated concierge service, 24-hour security, and valet parking ensure residents’ comfort and peace of mind.\n\nFortune 5 ensures that residents of the Marriott Residences at Business Bay will benefit from the legendary hospitality and service excellence. They create a unique living experience that combines the comforts of home with the finest amenities and services.\n\nBeyond its appeal as a prestigious living space, the Marriott Residences at Business Bay also present an attractive investment opportunity. With Dubai’s robust real estate market, these residences hold the potential for significant appreciation and strong rental yields, making them an appealing choice for investors seeking both capital growth and rental income.', 301, '21bd044fe194347efde0e4c5d7d9ad34', NULL, '', 0, '2026-10-08 06:41:26'),
(6325, 'blog', '171', 2, 'article', 'The Highly Anticipated Marriott Residences is All Set To Be Launched At Business Bay', 'our-blogs/marriott-residences-is-all-set-to-be-launched-at-business-bay', 'Blog: The Highly Anticipated Marriott Residences is All Set To Be Launched At Business Bay (published 2023-05-13)\nThe launch of the Marriott Residences at Business Bay by Fortune 5 marks an exciting milestone in Dubai’s luxury real estate market. Combining the prestige of the Fortune 5 with an exceptional location and world-class amenities, this development offers a unique opportunity to experience the epitome of upscale living in one of the city’s most sought-after districts. Whether as a primary residence or an investment property, the Marriott Residences at Business Bay represent the pinnacle of luxury and sophistication.', 158, '40ad249e72d48bb7ded5f8f814ad040c', NULL, '', 0, '2026-10-08 06:41:26'),
(6326, 'blog', '172', 0, 'article', 'Dubai Property Market Adjusts to New Realities as Supply Increases', 'our-blogs/dubai-property-market-adjusts-to-new-realities-as-supply-increases', 'Blog: Dubai Property Market Adjusts to New Realities as Supply Increases (published 2025-03-25)\nThe Dubai property market is currently experiencing a shift, with new trends emerging as supply increases and buyers gain more power over sellers.\n\nFor the first time in years, property buyers in the UAE seem to have the upper hand. Recent data shows a drop in prices, signalling a market where developers and sellers are willing to lower their prices. In the past, developers used incentives like high commissions to attract buyers, but even these efforts couldn\'t prevent the decline in some market sectors, especially in off-plan sales.\n\nWhile some commentators argue that this price drop is a temporary trend or that the data needs to be reconsidered, the reality is that prices have been falling for months in several areas. This price shift is largely driven by a growing supply of homes. With over 300,000 units expected to be delivered in the next four years, there are now more homes on the market than at any point in the last six years, even when adjusting for expected delivery rates.\n\nDevelopers Turn to Joint Ventures and Discounts\n\nWith lower competition and less urgency in the market, bidding wars are becoming less common. Developers are adapting by forming joint ventures with land banks to manage cash flow and offering larger discounts for upfront payments—strategies not seen in recent years.', 353, 'd2a36c05eaad91afd132235f0f46dcaa', NULL, '', 0, '2026-10-08 06:41:26'),
(6327, 'blog', '172', 1, 'article', 'Dubai Property Market Adjusts to New Realities as Supply Increases', 'our-blogs/dubai-property-market-adjusts-to-new-realities-as-supply-increases', 'Blog: Dubai Property Market Adjusts to New Realities as Supply Increases (published 2025-03-25)\nAs a result, properties are sitting on the market longer, with time on the market at its highest since February 2020. This shift is part of a global trend, seen in places like the US, where home sales have fallen despite low supply levels.\n\nIn Dubai, land prices have dropped for the first time, signaling a market correction. While some point to supply chain issues, the fact remains that prices had begun to exceed their actual replacement value. This imbalance, particularly between off-plan and ready properties, is now starting to correct.\n\nBuyers Gain the Upper Hand in Refurbishment and Ready Homes\n\nIn the refurbishment market, buyers are increasingly able to negotiate lower prices. Deals are falling through more often as buyers now have the power to walk away from inflated prices and choose sellers who are offering more realistic pricing.\n\nThe growing supply of new homes has made it possible to meet more than a year’s worth of demand, the highest level seen since the 2014 boom-bust cycle. For retail buyers, this means more options and better affordability. In areas like Jumeirah Lake Towers (JLT), the median price for ready homes is Dh1,530 per square foot, while off-plan homes are priced at Dh2,370. The pricing gap is even wider in places like the DubaiLand Residential Complex.\n\nInvestors and Speculators Adjust to the New Market', 362, 'e139d336d44780dd2824c513d04cbaad', NULL, '', 0, '2026-10-08 06:41:26'),
(6328, 'blog', '172', 2, 'article', 'Dubai Property Market Adjusts to New Realities as Supply Increases', 'our-blogs/dubai-property-market-adjusts-to-new-realities-as-supply-increases', 'Blog: Dubai Property Market Adjusts to New Realities as Supply Increases (published 2025-03-25)\nFor investors and speculators, the market is presenting new challenges. The financial risks associated with off-plan investments are becoming more apparent, as prices are adjusting to reflect the true value of properties. While some investors may have misjudged the market in the past, experienced buyers know that property cycles are inevitable and are now preparing for the next stage.\n\nThe Dubai property market is entering a new phase, with an increasing supply of homes, lower prices, and more power for buyers. This shift is reshaping the landscape, offering better opportunities for retail buyers and investors who are ready to adapt.\n\nSource: Gulf News', 189, '9d48836939e7567a45e0662f0935d10e', NULL, '', 0, '2026-10-08 06:41:26'),
(6329, 'blog', '173', 0, 'article', 'UAE Introduces New Dirham Symbol Inspired by the National Flag', 'our-blogs/uae-introduces-new-dirham-symbol-inspired-by-the-national-flag', 'Blog: UAE Introduces New Dirham Symbol Inspired by the National Flag (published 2025-03-28)\nIn a groundbreaking move, the UAE has unveiled a fresh symbol for its national currency, the Dirham, designed to reflect both the nation’s rich heritage and its forward-thinking financial future. On Thursday, the Central Bank of the UAE (CBUAE) revealed the new symbol, which will represent the Dirham in both physical and digital formats, highlighting the country’s commitment to innovation and global financial integration.\n\nThe new dirham symbol was carefully crafted from the English name of the currency, with two horizontal lines integrated into the design to represent stability—a key characteristic of the UAE’s dirham. These lines are inspired by the UAE flag, linking the symbol to the country’s national identity while embodying the values of financial strength and stability.\n\nThe digital version of the symbol includes a circle around the physical design, infused with the vibrant colors of the UAE flag. This digital adaptation not only represents the nation’s pride and patriotism but also signifies the UAE’s expanding global financial influence and its dedication to fostering a technologically advanced monetary ecosystem.', 308, '54431ca549a9cf3b75a2975cadebfb84', NULL, '', 0, '2026-10-08 06:41:26'),
(6330, 'blog', '173', 1, 'article', 'UAE Introduces New Dirham Symbol Inspired by the National Flag', 'our-blogs/uae-introduces-new-dirham-symbol-inspired-by-the-national-flag', 'Blog: UAE Introduces New Dirham Symbol Inspired by the National Flag (published 2025-03-28)\nThe new symbol seamlessly integrates the lines of the UAE flag into the letter “D” for Dirham, honoring the nation’s history while reimagining it in a modern context. The sleek, pointed curves in the design are reminiscent of classical Arabic calligraphy, such as the elegant Thuluth and Diwani scripts, which are known for their graceful, sweeping lines that evoke both authority and elegance.\n\nIncorporating the UAE’s bold national colors, the symbol ensures immediate recognition across both physical and digital platforms. This blend of tradition and innovation allows the Dirham to present a dynamic, forward-looking image while staying rooted in the nation’s identity.\n\nThe unveiling of the new dirham symbol coincides with the UAE’s growing efforts to modernize its currency and financial infrastructure. As part of these efforts, the UAE has also introduced the concept of the Digital Dirham—a digital version of the national currency that will use blockchain technology to ensure secure and efficient transactions.\n\nSet for release in the final quarter of 2025 for the retail sector, the Digital Dirham is designed to reduce transaction costs while enhancing security. Blockchain’s ability to provide effective risk management, data protection, and secure, instant transactions makes the Digital Dirham a significant step forward in the UAE’s financial evolution.\n\nKey Features of the Digital Dirham:', 376, '115fe12a6590aa4659cacc5eecb25508', NULL, '', 0, '2026-10-08 06:41:26'),
(6331, 'blog', '173', 2, 'article', 'UAE Introduces New Dirham Symbol Inspired by the National Flag', 'our-blogs/uae-introduces-new-dirham-symbol-inspired-by-the-national-flag', 'Blog: UAE Introduces New Dirham Symbol Inspired by the National Flag (published 2025-03-28)\nTokenization: The Digital Dirham enables tokenization, making it easier for individuals and businesses to access liquidity and participate in digital financial systems. This innovation also enhances financial inclusion by expanding access to digital assets and fractionalized investments.\n\nSmart Contracts: Through the Digital Dirham, users can leverage smart contracts, which automate complex transactions and enable real-time settlements. This functionality is particularly valuable for multi-party transactions with conditions or obligations.\n\nIntegrated Digital Wallet: To facilitate seamless transactions, the CBUAE has developed a secure digital wallet for both individuals and businesses. The wallet supports various financial transactions, including retail payments, cross-border transfers, and withdrawals. This feature is designed to provide a user-friendly experience while meeting the highest industry standards.\n\nA Vision for the Future: The Digital Dirham will be integrated into an evolving digital financial ecosystem. With its flexible platform, the UAE is positioning itself as a global leader in digital payments, driving the growth of a secure and innovative financial environment.\n\nStrengthening the UAE’s Position in the Global Market', 337, 'e0043ba0da30bc46203c245b372424f7', NULL, '', 0, '2026-10-08 06:41:26'),
(6332, 'blog', '173', 3, 'article', 'UAE Introduces New Dirham Symbol Inspired by the National Flag', 'our-blogs/uae-introduces-new-dirham-symbol-inspired-by-the-national-flag', 'Blog: UAE Introduces New Dirham Symbol Inspired by the National Flag (published 2025-03-28)\nThe UAE’s commitment to the global financial market was further highlighted by its recent decision to join the FX Global Code, making it the first central bank in the Arab region to do so. This move reflects the nation’s dedication to enhancing Dirham’s role in the global currency exchange market, promoting ethical practices, and ensuring transparency and professionalism within the industry.\n\nA Symbol of Progress and Stability\n\nThe new Dirham symbol not only reflects the UAE’s deep-rooted identity but also signals its determination to be at the forefront of global financial innovation. With the forthcoming launch of the Digital Dirham and other cutting-edge financial initiatives, the UAE continues to demonstrate its leadership in shaping the future of finance, both regionally and globally.\n\nSource: The Khaleej Times', 230, 'e9e26a613c1a04573ecee7250be3d09b', NULL, '', 0, '2026-10-08 06:41:26'),
(6333, 'blog', '174', 0, 'article', 'DAMAC and Chelsea FC Team Up for Dubai’s First Football-Inspired Luxury Residences', 'our-blogs/damac-and-chelsea-fc-team-up-for-dubais-first-football-inspired-luxury-residences', 'Blog: DAMAC and Chelsea FC Team Up for Dubai’s First Football-Inspired Luxury Residences (published 2025-05-02)\nIn a striking blend of sport and sophistication, Chelsea Football Club has partnered with Dubai-based luxury developer DAMAC Properties to unveil a groundbreaking concept: football-themed branded residences in the heart of Dubai.\n\nThe project, dubbed Chelsea Residences by DAMAC, marks the first time the iconic London club has lent its name and spirit to a real estate venture. Located in the prestigious Dubai Maritime City, the development will feature over 1,400 seafront apartments, complete with high-end Chelsea-branded amenities designed to promote health, fitness, and wellbeing.\n\nBut the collaboration goes far beyond architecture and interiors.\n\nIn a strategic move to amplify its global visibility, DAMAC’s logo will also appear on Chelsea’s men’s and women’s team kits for the rest of the 2024–25 football season. The branding will make its on-field debut during Chelsea’s UEFA Conference League semi-final match against Djurgården.\n\nThis partnership signals a powerful alignment of two globally recognized brands. For Chelsea FC, it’s a bold step in strengthening its presence in the Middle East a region where football passion runs deep and luxury living is a lifestyle standard. For DAMAC, it’s a natural progression from its past collaborations with elite fashion and luxury houses like Versace, Roberto Cavalli, and de GRISOGONO.', 365, '794b08b3d0c168ef9cbb675eee74604c', NULL, '', 0, '2026-10-08 06:41:26'),
(6334, 'blog', '174', 1, 'article', 'DAMAC and Chelsea FC Team Up for Dubai’s First Football-Inspired Luxury Residences', 'our-blogs/damac-and-chelsea-fc-team-up-for-dubais-first-football-inspired-luxury-residences', 'Blog: DAMAC and Chelsea FC Team Up for Dubai’s First Football-Inspired Luxury Residences (published 2025-05-02)\nAmira Sajwani, DAMAC’s Managing Director of Sales & Development, emphasized that this isn’t just another property launch — it’s a statement of excellence.\n\n“This initiative goes beyond celebrating the beautiful game; it sets a new benchmark for those who expect nothing less than the exceptional,” she said.\n\nEvery element of the residence will echo Chelsea’s DNA — from concierge services and exclusive lounges to cutting-edge training zones. The aim is to infuse Chelsea’s spirit of performance, legacy, and luxury into everyday living.\n\nChelsea FC President and COO Jason Gannon echoed this sentiment, adding: “Partnering with DAMAC allows us to bring the essence of Chelsea to life in Dubai — a city that mirrors our ambition, elegance, and innovation.”\n\nFounded in 2002, DAMAC has delivered over 48,000 homes globally, with tens of thousands more in the pipeline. With Chelsea Residences, the company is set to once again reshape Dubai’s skyline this time with a project where luxury meets loyalty.\n\nWhile full construction and pricing details are still under wraps, Chelsea Residences by DAMAC is set to be a standout on the Dubai skyline—an iconic project where luxury meets legacy.\n\nSource: Arabian Business', 332, '0f70b7b8243a2e1c3438979481767831', NULL, '', 0, '2026-10-08 06:41:26');

